# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# old_scrap/ holds a previous revision of this page. It stays in the repository
# because deleting the thing you replaced is how a correction stops being
# checkable — but it must not be REACHABLE, because a stale artifact served
# beside an approved one is a stale artifact served. Its index.html has already
# been renamed so no host will serve it as a page; this closes the directory
# itself. SHELL.md r6, hole 2.
/old_scrap/*  /  301

# The tools are in the deploy tree and Cloudflare Pages serves the tree, so
# launch-gate.mjs and break-harness.mjs were BEING SERVED. Two reasons that is
# wrong, and the second is the one that forced this:
#
#   1. they are not the site. Nobody asked wrand.cc for a build script.
#   2. THEY BOTH NAME EVERY RETRACTED CLAIM, because that is what a blocklist
#      and a break harness are made of. The r15 scan added on 2026-08-17 —
#      every published file, not just index.html — refused on its very first
#      run for exactly this, and it was right to. A retracted sentence is
#      served whether it arrives in a page or in a script.
#
# Skipping them inside the gate by name was the other option and it is worse:
# r10, an exemption written by the same hand as the page is not a check. This
# is the same mechanism the host actually obeys, so the only way to be exempt
# from the scan is to genuinely stop being served.
/launch-gate.mjs    /  301
/break-harness.mjs  /  301
